OL,3,GNEWSA1970s theatre 'not worth spending
OL,4,Amillions on'
OL,5,
OL,6,FSpending millions of pounds on a town's
OL,7,F"ageing" theatre, which opened in 1971,
OL,8,Fis not good value for money, a council
OL,9,Fhas said.
OL,11,FSwindon Borough Council member Matthew
OL,12,FVallender said while the Wyvern had
OL,13,Fbeen "at the heart" of the town's
OL,14,Fculture for more than 50 years, the
OL,15,Fauthority had to be "realistic" and
OL,16,Fdevelop the case for a modern,
OL,17,Fpurpose-built theatre.
OL,19,FHowever Jim Robbins, leader of the
OL,20,Fprevious Labour administration, accused
OL,21,Fthe Conservatives on the council of
OL,22,Fhaving a lack of ambition.
OL,23,APub: 13-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
